s":"hanging"},{"surface":"விசியுறு","parts":[{"text":"விசி","lemma":"விசி","gloss":"tightness"},{"text":"உறு","lemma":"உறு","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"tightly bound"},{"surface":"தண்ணுமை","parts":[{"text":"தண்ணுமை","lemma":"தண்ணுமை","gloss":"drum"}],"gloss":"drum"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வளி","parts":[{"text":"வளி","lemma":"வளி","gloss":"wind"}],"gloss":"wind"},{"surface":"பொரு","parts":[{"text":"பொரு","lemma":"பொரு","gloss":"beat"}],"gloss":"striking"},{"surface":"தெண்கண்","parts":[{"text":"தெண்கண்","lemma":"தெண்கண்","gloss":"clear drumhead"}],"gloss":"clear drumhead","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கேட்பின்","parts":[{"text":"கேள்","lemma":"கேள்","gloss":"hear"},{"text":"பின்","lemma":"பின்","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if heard"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அது","parts":[{"text":"அது","lemma":"அது","gloss":"that"}],"gloss":"that"},{"surface":"போர்","parts":[{"text":"போர்","lemma":"போர்","gloss":"war"}],"gloss":"war"},{"surface":"என்னும்","parts":[{"text":"என்னும்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"saying"}],"gloss":"saying"},{"surface":"என்னையும்","parts":[{"text":"என்னை","lemma":"என்னை","gloss":"my lord"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"my lord too"},{"surface":"உளனே","parts":[{"text":"உளன்","lemma":"உள்","gloss":"exists"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis particle"}],"gloss":"he exists"}]}],"literal":"Jewel adornment shining prominent curved waist / gentle collyrium-painted eyes bright forehead female dancer / 'Are there fighters too in your wide-spaced country?' thus / asking unceasingly, O king of the fighting army! / Like a snake that does not fear a striking stick, / young warriors too exist; not only that, / hanging in the common hall, the tightly bound drum's / clear head, if the wind strikes and it is heard, / saying 'that is war!', my lord too exists!","translation":"O king of the fighting army, who never ceases to ask the gentle, bright-foreheaded female dancer with collyrium-painted eyes and a waist adorned with shining jewels, 'Are there any fighters in your wide country?' There are young warriors here who, like a snake that does not fear the stick that strikes it, know no fear. Not only that, there is also my lord! If he but hears the wind beating against the clear skin of the tightly bound drum hanging in the common hall, he rises, saying, 'That is the sound of war!'","modern":"ஒளிரும் அணிகலன்கள் அணிந்த, உயர்ந்த அல்குலையும், மென்மையான தன்மையும், மை தீட்டிய கண்களையும், ஒளிரும் நெற்றியையும் உடைய விறலியே! 'உங்களுடைய அகன்ற நாட்டில் போரிடும் வீரர்கள் இருக்கிறார்களா?' என்று ஓயாமல் கேட்கும் போர்ப்படையை உடைய வேந்தனே! அடிக்கும் கோலுக்கு அஞ்சாத பாம்பைப் போன்ற இளைய வீரர்கள் இங்கு இருக்கிறார்கள். அதுமட்டுமல்லாமல், பொதுமன்றத்தில் தொங்கும், இறுக்கமாகக் கட்டப்பட்ட தண்ணுமையில் காற்று மோதி ஒலிக்கும் தெளிந்த ஓசையைக் கேட்டவுடனேயே, 'அது போர் முரசு' என்று கிளம்பும் என் தலைவனும் இருக்கிறான்!","explanation":"The poet Avvaiyar addresses an invading king who has patronizingly asked a female dancer (viṟali) whether there are any worthy fighters in her wide country, the domain of Atiyamāṉ Neṭumāṉ Añci. Avvaiyar proudly responds on behalf of her land. She tells the king that not only are there young, fierce warriors who, like angry snakes, do not fear any weapon, but there is also her great lord, Atiyamāṉ. He is so eager for battle that even when the wind merely brushes against the drum hanging in the common assembly hall, he mistakes it for the call to war and prepares to fight. This poem belongs to the tumpai tiṇai, which celebrates active warfare and the valor of soldiers, and the theme is tāṉai maṟam, the bravery of the army and its leader.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.3],[0.3,0.8],[0.8,0.8],[0.8,1.6],[1.6,2.0],[2.0,3.2],[3.2,3.2],[3.2,3.8],[3.8,4.1],[4.1,5.4],[5.4,5.5],[5.5,5.9],[5.9,6.2],[6.2,6.9],[6.9,7.3],[7.3,7.7],[7.7,8.0],[8.0,8.2],[8.2,8.7],[8.7,9.8],[9.8,10.0],[10.0,10.4],[10.4,10.7],[10.7,11.3],[11.3,11.5],[11.5,11.7],[11.7,12.2],[12.2,13.5],[13.5,13.7],[13.7,14.0],[14.0,14.6],[14.